1
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:17,180
Hi guys, I'm back and in today's video we are going to deal with one

2
00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:23,840
of the hardest, most painful questions in the
IELTS reading test, which is matching headings.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:27,680
So stay tuned and we'll dive right into it.

4
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:33,400
This lesson aims to help you understand some features of matching headings,

5
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:41,280
choose one effective approach to matching headings,
understand and apply steps for matching headings.

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,360
So hang in there, it'll be worth it, I promise.

7
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,460
We'll start with the first part of today's lesson.

8
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:58,440
Matching headings is a question type which requires candidates to match the

9
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:03,340
given headings with the paragraphs, so that each paragraph will be matched with

10
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,480
its corresponding heading.

11
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:16,800
Questions of matching headings often have three parts, a requirement,
a list of headings and question numbers corresponding to paragraphs.

12
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:22,400
Moreover, there are some features of matching
headings that you should pay attention to.

13
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:31,160
One heading is only used for one paragraph, there are no
cases where two or more paragraphs have the same heading.

14
00:01:31,990 --> 00:01:38,800
There are usually more headings than the number of
paragraphs, so there are some headings that are not used.

15
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:43,940
The correct headings need to cover the whole content of paragraphs.

16
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:51,180
These are the most basic features of this question
type, let's analyse it in more detail in the next part.

17
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:59,920
There are two approaches to matching headings that you can choose from.

18
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:07,039
Approach 1. Answer this question type right
from the beginning, because it usually appears

19
00:02:07,039 --> 00:02:11,900
as the first question type of one passage, usually in passage 2.

20
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:21,320
The advantage is that it helps us to understand the main idea of all
paragraphs, therefore we can answer the following question types faster.

21
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:28,080
However, the disadvantage is that it can take
us a lot of time from the beginning of the test.

22
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,820
As a result, it is difficult to manage time.

23
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:36,740
If we answer this question type for too long, we can take up a lot

24
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:42,060
of time for other questions and can't solve all the questions in time.

25
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,880
Approach 2. Answer this question type last.

26
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:52,500
The advantage is that we can finish this question type faster, because after

27
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:56,860
answering other question types, we can understand the main idea of the whole

28
00:02:56,860 --> 00:03:01,720
reading passage and can somehow understand the information in each paragraph.

29
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:05,900
So finding the main idea of each paragraph is faster.

30
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:13,540
The disadvantage is that we can't answer other question
types as quickly as we take the first approach.

31
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,180
Of course, the choice belongs to you.

32
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:25,040
Each of you can have an approach that you find effective,
so please choose the most suitable one for yourself.

33
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:29,440
Now let's see how we can handle the matching headings questions.

34
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:36,960
Now let's learn how to handle this question type step by step.

35
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:40,820
Step 1.
Read given headings and underline keywords.

36
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:44,460
In this step, we need to have an overview of the headings.

37
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:49,380
Because this question type often includes headings with similar keywords, you

38
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:54,640
need to take notes by circling or rewriting the
similarities or differences in your own language.

39
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:57,960
This helps us find out the correct headings more easily.

40
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:05,120
After you understand the importance of this step, I'll
give you 15 seconds to underline keywords in each heading.

41
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:09,020
Find out differences among the headings that contain similar keywords.

42
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,500
Here are the keywords I found when reading the headings.

43
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:33,920
When reading, I noticed that headings 5 and 6 both talk about education or

44
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:40,820
schools, but 5 focuses on different ways and
methods, while 6 focuses on success rates.

45
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:46,580
Similarly, headings 1 and 4 both mention the brain, but 1 is about old age

46
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:50,120
or health, and 4 is about focus and multitasking.

47
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:53,400
After having an overview, we move on to the next step.

48
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:59,220
Step 2. Use skimming skills for
each paragraph to find the main idea.

49
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,100
A quick tip.

50
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:06,740
In academic writing, the first sentence is often the topic
sentence, and the last sentence summarizes the ideas.

51
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:41,600
Let's analyze the content words to find the main idea.

52
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,360
This first sentence sets the context.

53
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:49,540
The key idea here is, speaking more than one language is becoming more common.

54
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,360
Now on to the second sentence.

55
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:55,340
This sentence explains why it is becoming common.

56
00:05:55,340 --> 00:06:00,660
Keywords include migration, global
communication, millions use different languages.

57
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:04,640
This sentence here reinforces the first point.

58
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:08,800
Keywords here are rare skill and normal part of life.

59
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:12,040
The final sentence summarizes the trend.

60
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:16,500
Keywords include specialized talent and essential everyday skill.

61
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:21,540
To sum up, we can see the main idea of paragraph A is about how

62
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:25,640
speaking multiple languages has grown from something rare to something very

63
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,580
common and essential globally.

64
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:32,620
Step 3. Choose the most suitable
heading for each paragraph.

65
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:37,780
Now let's look at our headings again and
choose the one that matches our main idea.

66
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,520
Let's check heading 3.

67
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:44,160
The paragraph talks about modern, connected world, migration, global

68
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:48,580
communication, and how it is becoming more common and a normal part of life.

69
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:51,560
This matches perfectly with global increase.

70
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:55,680
So the answer for paragraph A is 3.

71
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:59,120
Once found, cross it out to save time for the next paragraph.

72
